This repository holds ArchSim's own source only. What it builds bundles third-party open-source
software, each under its own license, which is not part of this repository's source. Each of
these licenses is compatible with the AGPL-3.0; where a library offers a choice, ArchSim takes
the one compatible with the GPL (docs/adr/0067-license-under-agpl-3.0-with-a-commercial-license.md):

- The API image (archsim-app, built with Jib), the command line (archsim-cli) and the MCP server
  (archsim-mcp) bundle these Java libraries:
  - under the Apache License 2.0: Spring Framework, Spring Boot and Spring Security, Apache
    Tomcat (embedded), Jackson, Flyway, HikariCP, Hibernate Validator, Micrometer,
    springdoc-openapi and Swagger UI, SnakeYAML, Apache HttpComponents (HttpClient 5), picocli,
    Project Reactor, the networknt JSON Schema validator, JSpecify, Apache Commons Lang and
    Logging, JBoss Logging, ClassMate, ethlo ITU, Nimbus JOSE+JWT, with the Gson library it
    bundles, the Nimbus OAuth 2.0 SDK with OpenID Connect extensions, Nimbus Content Type and
    Nimbus Language Tags, json-smart and accessors-smart, and the JCIP annotations (bundled in
    Nimbus JOSE+JWT, and on their own);
  - under the MIT License: the Model Context Protocol Java SDK, SLF4J, the Checker Framework's
    qualifiers and WebJars Locator Lite; Reactive Streams under MIT-0;
  - the PostgreSQL JDBC driver, under the BSD 2-Clause License, and ASM, under the BSD 3-Clause
    License;
  - Logback, under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 (of its EPL-2.0 or LGPL-2.1
    choice);
  - the Jakarta Annotations API, under the GNU General Public License 2.0 with the Classpath
    Exception (of its EPL-2.0 or GPL-2.0-with-Classpath-Exception choice), and the Jakarta Activation and XML Binding APIs, under the Eclipse
    Distribution License 1.0 (BSD 3-Clause).
  The NOTICE and license files these libraries carry are kept, unchanged, inside their jars.
- The web image (apps/web, Next.js's standalone output) bundles Next.js, React, React Flow
  (@xyflow/react), Zustand, Recharts, Radix UI, Sonner, clsx, class-variance-authority,
  tailwind-merge and their dependencies (MIT, ISC, Apache-2.0 and BSD licenses), styles built with
  Tailwind CSS (MIT), lucide-react (ISC), elkjs (GNU General Public License 3.0 or later, of its
  EPL-2.0 or GPL-3.0-or-later choice) and Simple Icons (CC0-1.0). Next.js draws a shared run's preview
  image with the @vercel/og and Satori it bundles, under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 and
  shipped unmodified; their source is at https://www.npmjs.com/package/@vercel/og and
  https://github.com/vercel/satori. The image leaves out sharp and the libvips that sharp
  bundles: the app turns off Next.js's image optimizer, their only user.
- The web UI uses the Geist and Geist Mono typefaces (SIL Open Font License 1.1), downloaded at
  build time and served by the app itself.
- The website (archsim.io, a static export of apps/web) ships a subset of the web app's client
  code and the same typefaces. Its pages are rendered from the repository's Markdown at build time
  with unified, remark, rehype and their dependencies (MIT and ISC) and highlight.js (BSD 3-Clause),
  none of which it ships.

The accuracy benchmarks' harness (archsim-benchmarks) and the repository's tools (archsim-tools)
are not part of ArchSim's product and ship in no image; the benchmarked services the harness
builds (benchmarks/service-*) install their own dependencies at build time.

Technology logos in the web UI come from Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org, CC0-1.0). The
logos are trademarks of their respective owners. ArchSim uses them only to identify the
technology a component is modelled after; this implies no endorsement, and the simulation
behaviour always comes from the numbers in the model, not from the product named.
